{
  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, singleprofile, scgpt, ViT-L, concat → 43.5% acc), evidence is very sparse and the baseline accuracy is low. The most important architectural uncertainty is whether the multiprofile + aggregation design (which allows the model to integrate multiple cellular profiles) can substantially outperform the singleprofile baseline. config_006 keeps the same RNA encoder (scgpt) and image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) as config_001 but switches to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation and concat fusion, isolating the effect of the profile/aggregation architecture. This is the best next experiment because: (1) it directly extends the only data point we have, making results interpretable; (2) multiprofile+aggregation is a major design axis that could unlock significant gains; (3) with 8 experiments remaining, establishing whether this architectural upgrade helps early will guide whether to invest further in multiprofile variants or pivot toward encoder/fusion changes."
}

